flowchart TD
    Patch["<b>1. patched function entry</b><br/>arch ftrace/BPF machinery turns<br/>NOP space into an entry call path<br/><b>handoff:</b> trampoline runs<br/>before the function body<br/><b>state:</b> original args still available"]

    Tramp["<b>2. BPF trampoline</b><br/>saves argument registers, builds<br/>the BPF calling convention<br/><b>handoff:</b> verifier-approved program<br/>expects typed args/ctx<br/><b>state:</b> BPF-visible args ready"]

    Prog["<b>3. fentry program</b><br/>observes filename_unlinkat args<br/>before unlink logic runs<br/><b>handoff:</b> return 0 continues<br/>kernel execution<br/><b>state:</b> optional event data prepared"]

    Event["<b>4. tracing side effect</b><br/>ringbuf or map update exposes<br/>observation to userspace<br/><b>handoff:</b> trampoline can restore<br/>normal execution<br/><b>state:</b> event recorded without<br/>changing syscall behavior"]

    Body["<b>5. original function body</b><br/>registers restored, filename_unlinkat<br/>performs lookup, permission checks, unlink<br/><b>state:</b> caller sees the normal<br/>kernel return value"]

    Patch --> Tramp --> Prog --> Event --> Body

    classDef hot fill:#ffe5b4,stroke:#d97706,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bpf fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb,stroke-width:2px
    classDef kern fill:#e5e7eb,stroke:#374151,stroke-width:2px
    class Patch,Tramp hot
    class Prog,Event bpf
    class Body kern
